            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type"} type
            now called (lawful)
            %em lenses
            \&amp;lbrack;
            %a{:href => "#BohannonPierceVaughan06"}> Bohannon, Pierce &amp; Vaughan (2006, §3)
            ,
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#FosterGreenwaldMoorePierceSchmitt07"} Foster, Greenwald, Moore, Pierce &amp; Schmitt (2007, §3)
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Oles82"} Oles 1982
            %a{:href => "#Oles86"} 1986
            and
            = succeed "&rbrack;" do
              %a{:href => "#HofmannPierce96"} Hofmann &amp; Pierce 1996
            = succeed "(" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/data"} data
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/database"} -base
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            equipped with a read/write functionality (only) for a specified view-type
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
          %p
            In particular, “very well-behaved” or “lawful” lenses (see Def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Lens"}
            below) – those for which updates of the “view”
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            completely overwrite any previous such changes – turn out to equivalently be data base types of product form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo =
                  %mi D
                  %mo ×
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S = D \times V
            with “view” given by projecting onto the
            = succeed "-factor." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            = succeed "):" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monads+in+computer+science"} monads in computer science
          %ul
